# AE-0347 — Round 2 External QA Review

## Round-1 finding verification

| R1 ID | Status | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| **M1** notes verbatim → translation prompt | **Fixed at source** | `sanitize_display_input` in `ContentDraftAgent._parse_draft` (agents/content_draft_agent.py:198) covers fresh drafts, cache replays (`_cached_raw` re-parses, :157), and the fail-closed retry path. DDD ratchet holds: `git diff origin/main..HEAD` shows zero new `rag_backend.agents` imports in application-layer files. |
| **M2** no observability on missing notes | **Fixed, weakened** | Named warning `content_draft.long_form_notes_missing` (agents/content_draft_agent.py:202-204); test asserts it fires. |
| **m1** magic string `"carousel"` | **Fixed & complete** | `BLOG_ORIGIN_CAROUSEL = BlogPostOrigin.CAROUSEL.value` (modules/publishing/infrastructure/public_visibility.py:18); enum value is identical `"carousel"` (domain/constants/blog_post.py:32) — no behavior change. All remaining `origin='carousel'` hits are docstrings only. |
| **m2** payload `slide_index` default 0 | **Fixed** | 1-based positional fallback (editorial_distribution_generation.py:87), consistent with the caption resolver (:49); test `test_payload_index_falls_back_to_position` discriminates. |
| **m3** intro chosen by list position | **Fixed** | Selection by resolved `slide_index == INTRO_SLIDE_INDEX` with first-dict fallback (editorial_distribution_pack.py:80-86); `test_intro_is_selected_by_slide_index_not_position` fails on the old behavior. |
| **m4** runner state-key wiring untested | **Fixed** | Runner reads `STATE_FIELD_RESEARCH_FINDINGS` (phase_artifact_runner.py:255-257); new test captures the built context and proves the mapping end-to-end. |
| **m5** translation prompt in `.py` | Deferred (accepted) | Unchanged in domain/constants/ai_agents.py:38-39. |

## New issues introduced by the delta

- **BLOCKER — integrity gate red (net-new suppression).** `state,  # type: ignore[arg-type]` at tests/unit/application/test_carousel_blog_body_ae0347.py:339. `bash scripts/ci/check-integrity.sh backend` → `FAIL: 1 net-new integrity blocker(s) … bounce to developer`. The suppression is avoidable: `CarouselWorkflowState` is a `TypedDict, total=False` (application/services/carousel/workflow_state.py:13) — annotate the state literal (or use `get_initial_carousel_state`) and drop the ignore. Per AE-0259, Dev Complete requires `check-integrity.sh` green; this was shipped red.
- **MAJOR — order-dependent test on the process-global AI cache.** `test_agent_renders_v5_and_keeps_notes` (test_carousel_blog_body_ae0347.py:88-106) uses the exact prompt `draft_slide(1, "Title", ["Point"])` also used throughout tests/unit/agents/test_content_draft_agent.py, whose note-less cached raws poison `AIResponseCache` (TTL 3600s). Deterministic repro: `uv run pytest tests/unit/agents/test_content_draft_agent.py tests/unit/application/test_carousel_blog_body_ae0347.py` → 1 failed (`KeyError: 'long_form_notes'`). The full suite (2512 passed) is green only because `test_outline_agent.py`'s autouse fixture clears the cache between the files — cross-file luck. The team knew (the "process-global" comment + distinct prompts on the two *new* tests) but left the third exposed; adopt the autouse `get_ai_response_cache().clear()` fixture pattern from test_content_draft_agent.py:13-16.

## Carry-over / residual minors

- **MINOR (M2 metadata):** the warning carries only `prompt_version` — no `slide_index`/`project_id`/`model_id`, so ops can't correlate which slide/project went note-less; and it double-fires per cache hit (validation parse in `_cached_raw` + main parse, content_draft_agent.py:118/:157).
- **MINOR (M1 legacy data):** sanitization covers newly generated notes only. `sanitize_slide_drafts` (workflow_state_sanitize.py:156-187) does **not** touch `long_form_notes`, so pre-fix persisted drafts replayed on resume still feed unsanitized notes verbatim into the prompt (editorial_distribution_generation.py:97-99). Threat is model-output (low), but the exact path M1 flagged remains open for legacy rows.
- **MINOR (Gherkin drift):** tests/features/carousel_blog_body_ae0347.feature:14 still asserts "carries the long_form_notes **verbatim**" — now false post-sanitization; and none of the r2 behaviors (sanitize-at-source, missing-notes warning, index fallback, intro-by-index) have scenarios, contrary to AE-0153 for behavior-changing fixes.

